# ── NEVER COMMIT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The forbidden-token config is private. Publishing a file that enumerates what
# must not be said is worse than the leak it prevents. It lives at
# ~/.config/re-denylist.toml, outside every git tree.
*denylist*
*.denylist.toml
scan-report*.json
gitleaks-report*.json
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Planning documents. They carry positioning, competitor framing, and figures
# measured by other people — none of which is a claim this repository is
# willing to make, and none of which serves a reader. Kept on disk, never
# published. A different failure mode from the block above, so a separate rule.
docs/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/
*.pyc
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
site/_build/
.vscode/
specimens/**/_generated/
